`C-03` (`/audiomodes` as a read) contradicts itself and has to be resolved
before anything else in §17 is trusted. §17.1 says CONFIRMED, from the
2026-09-10 hardware pass — the pass that was deleted from this repo for
leaking a real MAC address, so the evidence behind the verdict is gone. The
clean 2026-09-11 re-run of the same claim, same firmware and same schema, came
back INCONCLUSIVE: 200 OK, but a 9-10 byte body on both players instead of the
populated `<audiomode>` element the vendor sample shows.

So the spec currently asserts something whose evidence no longer exists, and
the only evidence that does exist disagrees with it. Find out why the body
differs — short body as "no audio modes on this model", versus a request shape
that was wrong in the re-run — before touching the row. Do not quietly merge
the newer verdict over the older one; a claim that was CONFIRMED from deleted
evidence is its own finding about how the register was kept.

