iOS: the app sometimes drops to a "wifi not connected" screen. Seen roughly
twice in ten sessions while using the iPhone as the everyday controller. The
whole interface disappears and is replaced by that screen, then recovers in
under two seconds and possibly under one, and everything works immediately
once it is gone. Nowhere near enough data for MOTIVATION, and it does not
resemble the Android problems — recovery is instant and nothing is lost.

Worth knowing what triggers it. If the BluOS IPA becomes available, check what
puts the app into that state: whether it is a real network event, a failed
request treated as a lost network, or a foreground/background transition.
Until then, record the count and the circumstances each time it happens.
